From c51b6fe7adc9faaca353e9831f9e5291afe2133f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Raychenko <denis.raychenko@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 06:21:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] star6c (infinity6c): use ARGB1555 instead of broken I4
 palette, fix alpha threshold

On ssc377d/infinity6c, the I4 palette-indexed compositing path (the
SoC-specific default in InitMSPHook()) renders OSD text as a washed-out
purple/magenta instead of its real colors. This is downstream of msposd
in the closed SigmaStar mi_rgn/mi_sys vendor blob that composites the
I4 palette onto YUV video - confirmed by an independent from-scratch
rebuild of this exact source still reproducing the same purple shift
through a different internal init path, ruling out anything in this
repo as the cause.

The already-present (but commented out) ARGB1555 fallback for
__INFINITY6C__ avoids the broken path entirely and renders correct
colors. It initially rendered glyphs as hollow outlines only, traced to
convertRGBAToARGB1555()'s alpha threshold (a > 199) discarding most of
the font PNG's anti-aliased fill pixels down to fully transparent -
lowered to a > 20 so real coverage stays visible.

Combined, these two changes are the complete, user-confirmed color fix
on real hardware (ssc377d + BL-M8812EU2, msposd built via the star6c
Makefile target).
---
 bmp/bitmap.c |  8 +++++---
 osd.c        | 10 +++-------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bmp/bitmap.c b/bmp/bitmap.c
index bb44aa0..e16b9a7 100644
--- a/bmp/bitmap.c
+++ b/bmp/bitmap.c
@@ -1715,9 +1715,11 @@ void convertRGBAToARGB1555(
 			// Convert to ARGB1555 format
 			uint16_t pixel = 0;
 
-			// Set alpha bit (1 bit)
-			if (a > 199) {		 // Assuming any alpha value above 127 is considered
-								 // opaque Needs  to be higher
+			// Set alpha bit (1 bit) - low threshold: ARGB1555 has no partial
+			// alpha, so any real coverage should stay visible instead of
+			// being dropped to fully transparent (was > 199, way too high,
+			// silently discarded most of the glyph fill, leaving only edges)
+			if (a > 20) {
 				pixel |= 0x8000; // Set the alpha bit (1 << 15)
 			}
 
diff --git a/osd.c b/osd.c
index 5b6f24b..878b770 100644
--- a/osd.c
+++ b/osd.c
@@ -2754,13 +2754,9 @@ static void InitMSPHook() {
 	PIXEL_FORMAT_BitsPerPixel = 4;
 
 #ifdef __INFINITY6C__
-	//if I4 is not supported ?? uncomment these for slower rendering
-	//PIXEL_FORMAT_DEFAULT = PIXEL_FORMAT_1555; // ARGB1555 format, 16 bits per pixel
-	//PIXEL_FORMAT_BitsPerPixel = 16;
-
-	//PIXEL_FORMAT_DEFAULT = PIXEL_FORMAT_I4; // PIXEL_FORMAT_I4 format, 4 bits per pixel
-	//PIXEL_FORMAT_BitsPerPixel = 4;
-#endif	
+	PIXEL_FORMAT_DEFAULT = PIXEL_FORMAT_1555; // ARGB1555 format, 16 bits per pixel
+	PIXEL_FORMAT_BitsPerPixel = 16;
+#endif
 
 #endif
 #if defined(_x86) || defined(__ROCKCHIP__)
